  "answer": "I couldn't find a past ticket reporting this exact problem: Quick Accent turning on Caps Lock when Backspace and Caps Lock are swapped in Keyboard Manager. The closest ticket, PowerToys#45936 (Quick Accent causing intermittent Shift lock), involves a different key and has no Keyboard Manager remap or known cause. PowerToys#22002 is also different. It involves Quick Accent popping up after a Caps Lock to Ctrl remap, not a lock key being enabled. Please file this as a new issue, or keep it open, with your exact remap, the Quick Accent activation key and the steps that reproduce it. Attach a bug report ZIP from the PowerToys tray. In the meantime, you can avoid it by disabling Quick Accent or by removing the Backspace/Caps Lock swap."
